<div class="zv-dentures-body-wrapper" id="dentures-details">
  <style>
    .zv-dentures-body-wrapper {
      max-width: 1200px;
      margin: 40px auto;
      padding: 0 20px;
      font-family: inherit;
      color: #17433C;
      line-height: 1.65;
    }
    .zv-dentures-section {
      background: #FFFFFF;
      border: 1px solid rgba(23, 67, 60, 0.12);
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 32px 28px;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(23, 67, 60, 0.04);
    }
    .zv-dentures-section h2 {
      font-size: 22px;
      font-weight: 800;
      color: #17433C;
      margin-top: 0;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
    }
    .zv-dentures-section p {
      font-size: 15.5px;
      color: #334e48;
      margin-bottom: 14px;
    }
    .zv-dentures-section p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }
    .zv-dentures-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 20px;
      margin-top: 20px;
    }
    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .zv-dentures-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
      .zv-dentures-section {
        padding: 24px 18px;
      }
    }
    .zv-dentures-card {
      background: #F7F9F8;
      border: 1px solid rgba(23, 67, 60, 0.08);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 20px;
    }
    .zv-dentures-card h3 {
      font-size: 17px;
      font-weight: 750;
      color: #17433C;
      margin-top: 0;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }
    .zv-dentures-card p {
      font-size: 14.5px;
      color: #49635d;
      margin: 0;
    }
    /* Steps Layout */
    .zv-step-item {
      display: flex;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 16px;
      padding: 16px;
      background: #F7F9F8;
      border-radius: 12px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }
    .zv-step-num {
      width: 36px;
      height: 36px;
      background: #17433C;
      color: #C6FA54;
      font-size: 16px;
      font-weight: 800;
      border-radius: 50%;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }
    .zv-step-content strong {
      display: block;
      font-size: 15.5px;
      color: #17433C;
      margin-bottom: 4px;
    }
    .zv-step-content span {
      font-size: 14px;
      color: #49635d;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }
    /* Specs Table */
    .zv-dentures-specs-table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin-top: 10px;
      font-size: 14.5px;
    }
    .zv-dentures-specs-table th,
    .zv-dentures-specs-table td {
      padding: 12px 14px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(23, 67, 60, 0.08);
      text-align: left;
    }
    .zv-dentures-specs-table th {
      color: #17433C;
      font-weight: 700;
      width: 35%;
      background: #F7F9F8;
    }
    .zv-dentures-specs-table td {
      color: #334e48;
    }
    /* Included List */
    .zv-included-list {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 0;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .zv-included-list li {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 12px;
      padding: 12px 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(23, 67, 60, 0.08);
      font-size: 15px;
      color: #334e48;
    }
    .zv-included-list li:last-child {
      border-bottom: none;
    }
    .zv-included-icon {
      color: #17433C;
      font-size: 18px;
    }
    /* Safety Notice Box */
    .zv-safety-notice {
      background: #FFF9F5;
      border-left: 4px solid #D97706;
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 16px 18px;
      margin-top: 14px;
      font-size: 13.5px;
      color: #78350F;
      line-height: 1.55;
    }
    /* FAQ Accordion */
    .zv-dentures-faq-item {
      background: #F7F9F8;
      border: 1px solid rgba(23, 67, 60, 0.08);
      border-radius: 12px;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      overflow: hidden;
      transition: all 0.2s ease;
    }
    .zv-dentures-faq-item[open] {
      background: #FFFFFF;
      border-color: rgba(23, 67, 60, 0.25);
      box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
    }
    .zv-dentures-faq-summary {
      padding: 16px 20px;
      cursor: pointer;
      font-weight: 750;
      font-size: 15px;
      color: #17433C;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      list-style: none;
      user-select: none;
    }
    .zv-dentures-faq-summary::-webkit-details-marker {
      display: none;
    }
    .zv-dentures-faq-summary::after {
      content: '+';
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: 400;
      color: #17433C;
      transition: transform 0.2s ease;
    }
    .zv-dentures-faq-item[open] .zv-dentures-faq-summary::after {
      content: '−';
    }
    .zv-dentures-faq-answer {
      padding: 0 20px 18px;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: #49635d;
      line-height: 1.6;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(23, 67, 60, 0.06);
      padding-top: 12px;
    }
  </style>

  <!-- SECTION 1: A NATURAL-LOOKING SMILE -->
  <section class="zv-dentures-section">
    <h2><span>🦷</span> 1. A Natural-Looking, Confident Appearance</h2>
    <p>
      Zavelyn Custom-Fit Home Dentures are crafted to replicate the natural shading, subtle translucency, and curvature of healthy adult teeth. Featuring an anatomically contoured pink gum base, they fit comfortably along the mouth's natural boundary to restore balanced lip and cheek fullness without the heavy, bulky feel of traditional acrylics.
    </p>
    <div class="zv-dentures-grid">
      <div class="zv-dentures-card">
        <h3>Natural Shade Matching</h3>
        <p>Formulated with realistic enamel-tone resin to give your smile an authentic, healthy brightness that looks natural in any lighting.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="zv-dentures-card">
        <h3>Contoured Gum Integration</h3>
        <p>The soft-finish base gently blends with natural gum contours, helping maintain natural facial volume and an appealing smile profile.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 2: HOW THE THERMAL-ADAPTIVE SYSTEM WORKS -->
  <section class="zv-dentures-section">
    <h2><span>✨</span> 2. How the Thermal-Adaptive Fitting System Works</h2>
    <p>
      Unlike rigid, generic one-size trays, Zavelyn utilizes thermal-adaptive molding technology. When submerged in warm water (140°F–160°F / 60°C–70°C), the included molding beads become flexible and completely clear, allowing you to create an accurate impression of your unique gum contours.
    </p>
    <p>
      Once positioned, gentle biting pressure adapts the material to your mouth. As it cools in water, it solidifies into an opaque, personalized cushion that provides secure suction without needing messy dental glue or daily pastes.
    </p>
    <div class="zv-dentures-grid">
      <div class="zv-dentures-card">
        <h3>Suction-Assisted Comfort</h3>
        <p>Maps smoothly over your alveolar ridge to minimize slipping and eliminate abrasive rubbing against sensitive gums.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="zv-dentures-card">
        <h3>100% Re-Moldable Design</h3>
        <p>If the first fit isn't completely comfortable, simply re-soften in warm water and adjust again until it feels just right.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 3: WHAT'S INCLUDED IN EACH SET -->
  <section class="zv-dentures-section">
    <h2><span>📦</span> 3. What's Included in Each Kit</h2>
    <p>Every single set contains everything required for immediate at-home fitting and daily hygienic maintenance:</p>
    <ul class="zv-included-list">
      <li><span class="zv-included-icon">✔</span> <strong>1 × Upper Denture Arch Tray:</strong> Anatomically shaped upper cosmetic teeth and gumline.</li>
      <li><span class="zv-included-icon">✔</span> <strong>1 × Lower Denture Arch Tray:</strong> Flexible, slimline lower cosmetic arch.</li>
      <li><span class="zv-included-icon">✔</span> <strong>1 × Thermal-Adaptive Molding Beads (50g):</strong> High-yield supply for initial molding and micro-adjustments.</li>
      <li><span class="zv-included-icon">✔</span> <strong>1 × Dual-Ended Adjustment Tool:</strong> Designed for precise gel smoothing and edge contouring.</li>
      <li><span class="zv-included-icon">✔</span> <strong>1 × Protective Travel Case:</strong> Ventilated, shatter-resistant case for clean storage.</li>
      <li><span class="zv-included-icon">✔</span> <strong>1 × Illustrated Step-by-Step User Guide:</strong> Easy-to-follow visual directions.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 4: STEP-BY-STEP HOW TO USE -->
  <section class="zv-dentures-section">
    <h2><span>🛠️</span> 4. Step-by-Step Fitting Guide</h2>
    <p>Achieve your custom at-home fit in four simple steps:</p>

    <div class="zv-step-item">
      <div class="zv-step-num">1</div>
      <div class="zv-step-content">
        <strong>Soften in Warm Water</strong>
        <span>Place 15–20 thermal molding beads into a bowl of warm water (approx. 140°F–160°F). In 60 to 90 seconds, the beads will turn completely clear and pliable.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="zv-step-item">
      <div class="zv-step-num">2</div>
      <div class="zv-step-content">
        <strong>Line the Denture Channel</strong>
        <span>Using the adjustment tool or a clean spoon, lift the softened gel and press it evenly into the inner groove of the denture tray.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="zv-step-item">
      <div class="zv-step-num">3</div>
      <div class="zv-step-content">
        <strong>Position & Mold</strong>
        <span>Place the tray gently over your teeth and gums. Close your mouth and bite down with steady, moderate pressure for 60 seconds to mold the gel around your gumline.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="zv-step-item">
      <div class="zv-step-num">4</div>
      <div class="zv-step-content">
        <strong>Cool & Set</strong>
        <span>Remove the denture carefully and submerge it in a glass of cold water for 2–3 minutes. The gel will turn solid white and hold your custom shape.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 5: SPECIFICATIONS -->
  <section class="zv-dentures-section">
    <h2><span>📋</span> 5. Product Specifications</h2>
    <table class="zv-dentures-specs-table">
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th>Product Name</th>
          <td>Zavelyn Custom-Fit Home Dentures</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Application Type</th>
          <td>Removable At-Home Thermal Molding Cosmetic Kit</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Upper Arch Width</th>
          <td>Approx. 5.8 cm / 2.28 in (Adjustable contour)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Lower Arch Width</th>
          <td>Approx. 5.0 cm / 1.97 in (Adjustable contour)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Materials</th>
          <td>Food-Grade Thermal-Adaptive Polymer & Dental Cosmetic Resin (BPA-Free, Non-Toxic)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Storage Case Size</th>
          <td>19.4 cm × 10.3 cm × 2.7 cm (7.64 in × 4.06 in × 1.06 in)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Kit Net Weight</th>
          <td>Approx. 150g (Complete kit with accessories and packaging)</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 6: SAFETY, CARE & ORAL HYGIENE -->
  <section class="zv-dentures-section">
    <h2><span>🛡️</span> 6. Safety, Maintenance & Proper Care</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Daily Maintenance:</strong> Remove after wearing and rinse thoroughly under lukewarm water. Gently clean with a soft toothbrush and mild non-abrasive liquid soap or an approved denture soak. Store dry in the provided ventilated case. Do not submerge in boiling water or use abrasive bleaching agents.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Eating Recommendations:</strong> Suitable for everyday speaking, smiling, and light soft-to-medium foods. To preserve the fit and prevent unexpected detachment, do not consume sticky candies, hard nuts, ice cubes, or tough meats while wearing cosmetic dentures.
    </p>
    <div class="zv-safety-notice">
      <strong>Important Health Disclaimer:</strong> Zavelyn Custom-Fit Home Dentures are a removable cosmetic accessory intended for temporary aesthetic improvement. They are not a dental prosthesis, implant, or medical device, and they do not replace comprehensive dental care. This product does not prevent jawbone shrinkage, cure oral ailments, or restore clinical biting force. Discontinue use immediately if you experience gum irritation or ongoing discomfort, and consult a licensed dentist for underlying oral health concerns.
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 7: FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS -->
  <section class="zv-dentures-section">
    <h2><span>❓</span> 7. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <details class="zv-dentures-faq-item">
      <summary class="zv-dentures-faq-summary">What comes in one complete kit?</summary>
      <div class="zv-dentures-faq-answer">
        Each kit includes 1 Upper Denture, 1 Lower Denture, a 50g jar of thermal molding beads, a dual-ended fitting tool, an illustrated instruction booklet, and a compact protective travel case.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="zv-dentures-faq-item">
      <summary class="zv-dentures-faq-summary">Does it include both upper and lower dentures?</summary>
      <div class="zv-dentures-faq-answer">
        Yes! Every single set is a complete pair containing both the upper arch and lower arch.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="zv-dentures-faq-item">
      <summary class="zv-dentures-faq-summary">How does the fitting process work?</summary>
      <div class="zv-dentures-faq-answer">
        Simply soften the thermal beads in warm water (140°F–160°F) until clear, place the softened gel into the denture groove, and bite down gently for 60 seconds. Place in cold water for 2–3 minutes to set firmly.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="zv-dentures-faq-item">
      <summary class="zv-dentures-faq-summary">Can I adjust or remold them again if the fit isn't right?</summary>
      <div class="zv-dentures-faq-answer">
        Yes. The thermal molding gel is fully reusable. If you experience uneven pressure or want to tweak the fit, simply place the denture back in warm water to soften and remold.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="zv-dentures-faq-item">
      <summary class="zv-dentures-faq-summary">How should I clean and store the dentures?</summary>
      <div class="zv-dentures-faq-answer">
        Rinse thoroughly with lukewarm water after use and brush gently with a soft toothbrush. Store them in the supplied ventilated case when not in use. Avoid hot or boiling water.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="zv-dentures-faq-item">
      <summary class="zv-dentures-faq-summary">Can I eat while wearing these dentures?</summary>
      <div class="zv-dentures-faq-answer">
        They are suitable for speaking, smiling, and consuming softer everyday meals. We recommend avoiding tough steaks, hard crusts, sticky candies, or crunchy items while wearing them.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="zv-dentures-faq-item">
      <summary class="zv-dentures-faq-summary">What is the return policy for this product?</summary>
      <div class="zv-dentures-faq-answer">
        Every purchase is covered by Zavelyn's standard 30-Day Customer Guarantee. In accordance with federal hygiene and health standards for oral-use personal care items, returns and refunds are honored for new, unopened, and sealed packages, or verified manufacturing defects.
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>
</div>

